    "Fabrics of Late Antique African Red Slip Ware from North Tunisian Production Sites:",
    "The fabric characterization of African Red Slip Ware (ARS) from the North Tunisian production sites of Bordj el Djerbi (ARS D1), Henchir el Biar (ARS D1), Oudna (ARS D2), and Pheradi Maius (ARS C/D) is based on the survey material of the Dutch archaeologist Jan Willem Salomonson, who prospected ARS potteries in Tunisia in the 1960s and 1970s."
